{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact cut-short read head 34042856b98ad5e7e6523d7fcc8574a8aec51c6a on builder/cut-short-read-20261102, for request e4d0cfed and review request f4a93e37.\n\nScope. The source commit ebc1e608 sits directly on main 08a16dc6. The head adds three commits and changes 9 paths: session.ts, types.ts, browser/main.ts, the generated module, views-host.ts, view-sessions.test.ts, views-browser.mjs, and the note and manifest. After ebc1e608, only the note and the manifest change. The worktree is clean, and the commit-message check passes for all three commits. Every other live artifact at the head's paths sits on main.\n\nThe defect and the fix. #readExact now replays a retained answer only when that answer is complete: the lookup adds !item.shown.truncated. A truncated answer stays displayed with its cutoff text, commits, omitted-data words and reached file actions, and the next press goes through the existing read port. That press crosses the same active-view, cut, busy, offered-read and unresolved-original checks. The service then repeats its fresh authority, target, captured-view, signing, custody and credential checks. A new answer replaces the earlier entry with the same key, so retention stays bounded at four distinct reads. Reading or refreshing the view never retries a signed read.\n\nThe held branch no longer ignores #showRead. #showRead builds the checked projection before it changes any state, so a refused fit leaves page, cut and current read untouched. The press then returns an error that names the read and says \"the card cannot hold the retained answer. No new request was signed.\" It spends no credential and does not claim held:true. A later replay that fits clears only that receipt. That names what happens when the card cannot hold the answer, as e4d0cfed asks.\n\nThe browser control enables the current reader only while its shown answer is truncated, and a lone View diff keeps its reader control on the diff page for that case. A complete current reader stays disabled, and aria-current stays.\n\nThe witnesses. The session owner adds two cases. In the first, a stopped interdiff with no reached paths shows the cutoff words, the next press calls the port a second time and shows the complete answer, and the replay after going back returns held:true with no third call. In the second, the same complete answer no longer fits after the summary grows: the result is an error with the new receipt, page and cut stay put, and no call runs. Once the summary shrinks, replay succeeds and the receipt clears. The browser owner runs the stopped-diff fixture at 592 and 320 pixels through the production bridge, service, session, signer and custody. The first press signs one read-token act and shows the bound, the ordinary press signs a second and shows the complete answer, and the replay stays at two. Three named controls fail at their expected assertions:\n\n- Reusing truncated answers fails the two-call expectation.\n- Ignoring the fit result fails the isError assertion.\n- Disabling the current truncated reader fails \"The current stopped read can run again\" with no timeout.\n\nrestored.json records exact source and generated-module bytes afterwards.\n\nGate and CI. gate.exit at ebc1e608 reads 0. The source guards before and after match head ebc1e608, tree 365e708a, with clean status and the same lock hash. The terminal output shows 3,567 plain passes with one skip and 1,029 Native passes with two skips. Card workflow 41433119112 succeeds at exact ebc1e608: the generated-module check and all three browser steps pass. Only documentation follows, so no further run is due.\n\nEvidence. The manifest hashes to e251530e…fc8a, as the request states. All 139 files in its 6 units match their sizes and digests, no unit holds an unlisted file, and each unit's SHA256SUMS matches its manifest hash and passes. All 13 table digests match manifest entries. Two of them are the empty-output hash, for the compiler and the syntax check. No evidence file is writable, and the credential-pattern scan finds no match.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The decision lives in the view session, which owns retention and dispatch, and the rule \"only a complete answer replays\" uses the answer's own truncated flag instead of parsing provider words. The browser change is one condition on an existing control.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Each retry is a new press through the full signing and custody path, which is the intended cost. A replay or a refused fit signs nothing. Repository text still renders as text.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nLimits stay explicit: another press offers another bounded attempt and does not promise completion. The head changes no producer limits or omitted-data words, no renderer design (353a0ec0), and no Desktop or hosted outcome (1a44f042). The planner owns any deploy.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:38f0b2ca5a460215d1094816187904c5051cecf1","binding":"assigned","head":"34042856b98ad5e7e6523d7fcc8574a8aec51c6a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eae048647ccda8e747da96f7a039305909bb1236\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c43e2ff3f88921fde1b3f00295f60c39512aa394\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eae048647ccda8e747da96f7a039305909bb1236","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}